                                "sense_id": "e9716158-dabf-38ee-ae62-4f5e0711d833",
                                "text": "Being ruffled and the fur of his sensibilities being rubbed wrongwise by Wagner's exasperating din, he said as much to the audience generally from his place in the box."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c82dd7df-9070-4d48-993d-d6fb06c6872d",
                                "sense_id": "e9716158-dabf-38ee-ae62-4f5e0711d833",
                                "text": "It is to be feared that even this slight submission by the lofty Mr. Rea rubbed measurably wrongwise the vain fur of his self-love."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83efec37-5ad6-4ece-8865-863844a74f75",
                                "sense_id": "e9716158-dabf-38ee-ae62-4f5e0711d833",
                                "text": "With anie Mark at all; —noe, let him not\nMy Parchment wrongwise fold, nor stamp, nor blot, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89ad6042-96d2-4927-82b7-d8f5f9aa426c",
                                "sense_id": "e9716158-dabf-38ee-ae62-4f5e0711d833",
                                "text": "“Up one level, follow wrongwise until—here, I'll write out the directions; they're a bit involved.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
